 "content_notes": "Tone: absurd and ironic; the joke is on the smugglers' disguises, never on the people being smuggled, who are never drawn as a joke and stay out of frame (the narration says only that they were found; the card says detained, as reported). No weapon is drawn or pointed and no violence is shown; agents and officers hold only flashlights. The fence-cutter is an anonymous dark silhouette; the charged K-9 case defendants and the El Paso suspects are never named or drawn. Agents and officers are generic figures with no badge, patch, flag or agency seal. The fake trucks carry only plain lettering ('BORDER PATROL', 'K-9') and a plain green stripe, as the reported fakes did: no real seal, crest or plate number (the copied plate is drawn as blank dots). FedEx is plain text only: the vans are plain white with no logo, colours or artwork; nothing implies the company had any part. Every card is our own typed graphic. No dialogue or quotation. Facts verified 2026-10-18.",
